# Dev server testing

After making changes, ask the user whether they would like to run the dev server to test them.
For example: "Would you like me to run the dev server so you can test these changes?"
If the user has already asked to run it, start it without asking again and share the working URL.

Always use port 5173 for the web dev server and open localhost URLs on that port.
If port 5173 is occupied, ask the user whether you may stop the process using it and restart the dev server on 5173. Never automatically kill that process or switch to another port.

Use port 8080 for ember-api and port 8082 for ember-agents during local testing.
The user authorizes replacing the process occupying port 8080 when needed to run ember-api there. Identify the process before stopping it and restart the API on 8080 rather than selecting another port.
